MojoProof GPU run records: notice for the files in tests/gpu/

Each directory <kernel>/ holds a record of a GPU run of a corpus kernel (record.txt), the file the
run wrote (dump.txt: its inputs and outputs) and the test driver it ran. The records are conformance
tests, not proofs: tests/gpu/Compare.lean runs the grid evaluator on the inputs of the dump and
compares its output buffer with the GPU's. The directories mma/, ldmatrix/ and cp-async/ hold
records of one instruction each, not of a corpus kernel. Each has its own Compare.lean, which
compares the dump with the library's model of the instruction (MojoProofTest/TensorCoreGpu.lean,
MojoProofTest/AsyncGpu.lean), and its own NOTICE for its driver, a modified copy of Modular's
test_wmma.mojo, test_ldmatrix.mojo and test_async_cpy_wait_group.mojo.

The drivers are modified copies of Modular's code. Each keeps Modular's header, which reads:

    Copyright (c) 2026, Modular Inc. All rights reserved.

    Licensed under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions:
    https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt

and says in a comment what was changed: the imports of its origin are kept (for the vector
kernels also its declarations and kernel; the naive matmul kernel is imported, as there), and its
`main` is replaced by one that runs the kernel on random inputs at several launch sizes and
writes the dump. The license text is in tests/corpus/LICENSE-APACHE-LLVM.

